# Non-Nix catalog (package authors + monorepo teams)

Shipped: `modules/non-nix/catalog.toml`. Team extras:
`modules/non-nix/catalog.local.toml` (committed in monorepos; gitignored in
this publisher checkout; start from repo-root `catalog.local.toml.example`).
Same `[[tool]]` shape. Do not reuse a shipped `name`.

CLI tools install via mise (or Nix when `versionAtLeast` + homepage identity
match). Docker images and the devenv VS Code extension share the catalogs
but are not mise `[tools]`.

## Every `[[tool]]` needs a docs comment

Immediately above each `[[tool]]`, put **one** `#` line that states what the
tool does and points at upstream docs (URL or docs site path). Pin bumps must
not strip those comments (`catalog_set_pin` is line-local on purpose).

```
# ❌ BAD — bare table, no purpose or docs pointer
[[tool]]
name = "serena"
pin = "1.7.0"

# ✅ GOOD
# Code-memory MCP (symbol graph) for Cursor. Docs: https://oraios.github.io/serena/
[[tool]]
name = "serena"
kind = "cli"
scope = "user"
pin = "1.7.0"
mise = "pipx:serena-agent"  # installs via uv when uv is on PATH
```

## Add / remove entries

Prefer the flag-first tasks (docs comment via `--docs`, no leading `#`):

```
# ✅ GOOD — monorepo: non-nix:add-local / non-nix:remove-local
# ✅ GOOD — publisher: non-nix:add / non-nix:remove (needs includes/update/)
# ❌ BAD — hand-edit generated mise.toml or reuse a shipped name in catalog.local.toml
```

## Pins

```
# ❌ BAD — edit generated mise.toml or override a shipped name in catalog.local.toml

# ✅ GOOD — shipped pin: includes/update/non-nix.sh (publisher `update`)
# ✅ GOOD — team pin: modules/non-nix/catalog.local.toml + consumer `update`
```

`update` in this checkout runs shipped refreshers. In a consumer tree it runs
`devenv update`, then `modules/update/local-catalog.sh` (bump local pins;
Nix when promotable, else `mise install`).
